1
00:00:44,252 --> 00:00:47,964
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

2
00:01:16,910 --> 00:01:19,579
No. No.

3
00:01:35,011 --> 00:01:35,845
Baraka.

4
00:01:42,477 --> 00:01:43,520
Baraka.

5
00:01:46,898 --> 00:01:48,316
One, two, three, four…

6
00:02:00,411 --> 00:02:01,412
Baraka.

7
00:02:02,247 --> 00:02:03,289
Baraka?

8
00:02:03,373 --> 00:02:04,874
Wake up.

9
00:02:06,376 --> 00:02:07,293
Baraka…

10
00:02:51,921 --> 00:02:53,840
No!

11
00:02:58,970 --> 00:03:01,014
Ms. Jang Hui-suk.

12
00:03:02,182 --> 00:03:03,433
Ms. Jang Hui-suk.

13
00:03:10,732 --> 00:03:11,858
The meat's going to burn.

14
00:03:11,941 --> 00:03:13,276
EPISODE 4

15
00:03:20,700 --> 00:03:22,577
Have I done something wrong?

16
00:03:23,786 --> 00:03:25,830
I don't know. You tell me. Have you?

17
00:03:25,914 --> 00:03:28,541
- No.
- You're acting like you have.

18
00:03:28,625 --> 00:03:29,792
No, I haven't.

19
00:03:29,876 --> 00:03:31,127
Come on. Dig in.

20
00:03:36,341 --> 00:03:37,175
Here.

21
00:03:38,384 --> 00:03:40,178
He can barely do an appendectomy, right?

22
00:03:40,845 --> 00:03:42,513
- Who?
- Well, who do you think?

23
00:03:43,097 --> 00:03:44,140
My name's Na Dae-il.

24
00:03:44,224 --> 00:03:46,309
I'll be joining the hospital
as a general surgeon as of today.

25
00:03:47,185 --> 00:03:48,061
Pleasure to meet you.

26
00:03:54,108 --> 00:03:56,402
The contract is on hold for now.

27
00:04:01,157 --> 00:04:04,118
Dr. Na has served his country
for a long time

28
00:04:04,202 --> 00:04:08,081
as a career military doctor,
after which he worked in the States,

29
00:04:08,164 --> 00:04:11,584
and has now come running
to answer his alma mater's call.

30
00:04:11,668 --> 00:04:14,045
He's such a fantastic surgeon.

31
00:04:14,587 --> 00:04:19,300
Dr. Gye I'd like you to remain in the ER
to help out. We're always short-staffed.

32
00:04:19,384 --> 00:04:21,177
MEDICAL SERVICE RATE SHEET

33
00:04:24,430 --> 00:04:28,643
Plenty of trauma cases in the military,
so at least he'll be decent at stitching.

34
00:04:28,726 --> 00:04:29,769
He's pretty good, actually.

35
00:04:30,353 --> 00:04:31,562
- You've seen his work?
- Mm-hmm.

36
00:04:32,188 --> 00:04:33,815
- A liver transplant.
- A liver?

37
00:04:34,983 --> 00:04:37,694
I still can't believe
they stuck you in the ER

38
00:04:37,777 --> 00:04:39,279
after saving someone's life

39
00:04:39,362 --> 00:04:41,823
and rescuing them from a PR nightmare.

40
00:04:42,490 --> 00:04:44,284
After which, they held a press conference

41
00:04:44,367 --> 00:04:47,453
and put out a statement
taking credit for the whole thing.

42
00:04:47,537 --> 00:04:50,123
Auntie! Can I get
some more <i>ramyeon </i>noodles, please?

43
00:04:50,206 --> 00:04:52,917
- Auntie.
- <i>Ramyeon </i>noodles? Go ahead, order some.

44
00:04:53,001 --> 00:04:54,752
Hurry up and eat.
They could page you any second.

45
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:57,380
- Um, excuse me!
- No drinking.

46
00:04:57,880 --> 00:05:00,133
None at all, even if you can't sleep.

47
00:05:02,010 --> 00:05:03,052
I want you to know…

48
00:05:04,137 --> 00:05:05,305
this is <i>omija</i>.

49
00:05:06,264 --> 00:05:08,433
It's from Eung-gu. It's my pacifier.

50
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:10,643
Go ahead, smell it. Come on.

51
00:05:11,269 --> 00:05:12,645
We can't go back to that way of life.

52
00:05:13,855 --> 00:05:14,731
It's not right.

53
00:05:21,404 --> 00:05:23,072
Give me your coat. You're dripping on it.

54
00:05:28,911 --> 00:05:30,580
Don't get into trouble, okay?

55
00:05:30,663 --> 00:05:32,165
You're such a nag.

56
00:05:33,624 --> 00:05:34,917
Just lay low for now.

57
00:05:35,668 --> 00:05:36,836
They'll let you do surgeries again.

58
00:05:46,554 --> 00:05:47,388
Su-jeong!

59
00:05:54,354 --> 00:05:55,188
Stand up tall.

60
00:05:55,813 --> 00:05:57,106
Remember, you're Gye Su-jeong.

61
00:05:57,190 --> 00:05:59,400
Raised by me, Jang Hui-suk.

62
00:06:14,832 --> 00:06:17,293
Pay us what you owe,
or I'll sue your pants off.

63
00:06:20,296 --> 00:06:21,506
I'll leave the melon for you.

64
00:06:21,589 --> 00:06:23,424
I'm sure you'll be calling me soon.

65
00:06:24,926 --> 00:06:25,885
It was nice meeting you.

66
00:06:30,598 --> 00:06:32,892
Such a good-looking guy.

67
00:06:36,854 --> 00:06:40,817
Yeesh. I wonder where they found
that shady bastard?

68
00:06:43,027 --> 00:06:46,197
Oh, that's the doctor
with the odd nickname.

69
00:06:46,280 --> 00:06:49,450
Oh, we were pretending not to see her,
but you must not have picked up on it.

70
00:06:50,910 --> 00:06:53,704
I never got to properly introduce myself
in the director's office.

71
00:06:54,205 --> 00:06:55,456
I've heard a lot about her, though.

72
00:06:56,416 --> 00:06:57,291
I think I'll say hello.

73
00:06:57,375 --> 00:06:59,460
No, no, she's not in our department.

74
00:06:59,544 --> 00:07:00,670
She won't return your greeting.

75
00:07:01,629 --> 00:07:03,881
There are a lot of things she won't do.

76
00:07:16,769 --> 00:07:17,854
Gye Su-jeong…

77
00:07:25,153 --> 00:07:26,529
- Put it down, put it down.
- Calm down.

78
00:07:26,612 --> 00:07:28,781
- No, just relax! Put the knife down!
- Put the knife down. Now!

79
00:07:28,865 --> 00:07:30,074
Put it down! Put it down!

80
00:07:34,996 --> 00:07:37,915
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

81
00:07:39,542 --> 00:07:42,753
Unbelievable! You had me talk to a patient

82
00:07:42,837 --> 00:07:46,424
so he could ask me a question
about something he read on the internet?

83
00:07:46,507 --> 00:07:47,675
You playing games?

84
00:07:47,758 --> 00:07:51,012
How dare you waste my valuable time
by having me talk to a patient!

85
00:07:52,054 --> 00:07:55,308
- Get out. Get out of here, you idiot.
- I'm so sorry.

86
00:07:55,391 --> 00:07:57,477
Uh… I apologize.

87
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:12,617
You sure are full of energy
so early in the morning,

88
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:14,410
Dr. Mun Yeong-jong.

89
00:08:16,787 --> 00:08:18,873
Gotten pretty full of yourself,
huh, Na Dae-il?

90
00:08:18,956 --> 00:08:21,125
- Hmm.
- Took you long enough to come see me.

91
00:08:21,209 --> 00:08:22,251
Why is that?

92
00:08:22,335 --> 00:08:25,129
Oh, things have been so hectic.
Sorry about that.

93
00:08:26,297 --> 00:08:28,966
From being your student, I know how much
talking to patients annoys you.

94
00:08:29,050 --> 00:08:30,801
I guess that kid just didn't get the memo.

95
00:08:30,885 --> 00:08:33,137
I was already pissed off
because I had to work the night shift.

96
00:08:34,263 --> 00:08:36,390
If they just shut up
and let me get on with it,

97
00:08:36,474 --> 00:08:38,726
I'll do the surgery and save their lives.

98
00:08:38,809 --> 00:08:42,104
They don't know crap, but they
sure are happy to talk my ear off.

99
00:08:42,188 --> 00:08:43,481
Why do they do that? Geez.

100
00:08:45,358 --> 00:08:46,400
Why are you here?

101
00:08:47,485 --> 00:08:49,487
Oh, right.

102
00:09:01,123 --> 00:09:03,876
So, have you had breakfast?

103
00:09:10,341 --> 00:09:11,425
Oh.

104
00:09:14,303 --> 00:09:18,140
Looks like he's been out for a while.
Yep, it's ice cold.

105
00:09:18,808 --> 00:09:21,435
Park Tae-gyeong. Hey, Park Tae-gyeong.

106
00:09:21,936 --> 00:09:23,646
Why is he sweating so much in his sleep?

107
00:09:24,689 --> 00:09:25,523
Dr. Park Tae-gyeong?

108
00:09:27,775 --> 00:09:29,193
Dr. Park Tae-gyeong.

109
00:09:35,366 --> 00:09:36,659
Don't worry. I'm okay.

110
00:09:36,742 --> 00:09:39,745
Were you actually sleeping
or just resting your eyes? Dude.

111
00:09:39,829 --> 00:09:41,247
Both at the same time.

112
00:09:41,956 --> 00:09:44,500
First thing I heard was,
"Yup, it's ice cold,"

113
00:09:44,584 --> 00:09:46,502
but I missed the right moment to get up.

114
00:09:47,086 --> 00:09:49,714
I never thought you would check my pupils.

115
00:09:49,797 --> 00:09:52,174
Oh, you were unresponsive
with a slight fever.

116
00:09:52,883 --> 00:09:55,136
- Sorry, buddy.
- No worries.

117
00:09:55,219 --> 00:09:57,972
I dreamed I was doing an ABGA
and the artery ruptured.

118
00:09:58,055 --> 00:09:59,599
There was blood everywhere.

119
00:09:59,682 --> 00:10:03,185
Oh, well,
no wonder you broke out in cold sweat.

120
00:10:03,269 --> 00:10:04,854
I've had the same dream you had.

121
00:10:04,937 --> 00:10:07,440
Only it wasn't a dream.

122
00:10:07,523 --> 00:10:10,401
What? Then you were the patient?

123
00:10:11,277 --> 00:10:14,238
Damn. I swear, this batch of interns
are all thumbs.

124
00:10:14,322 --> 00:10:16,282
Just like the good old days.

125
00:10:17,575 --> 00:10:19,994
Actually, my arm wasn't
the worst casualty.

126
00:10:20,494 --> 00:10:23,331
My partner looked like
he might need a blood transfusion.

127
00:10:24,206 --> 00:10:26,500
The human body has so much blood in it…

128
00:10:27,335 --> 00:10:30,212
On days like today, you need
something like <i>seonji </i>hangover soup.

129
00:10:30,296 --> 00:10:32,548
But first, throw that cold <i>ramyeon </i>away.

130
00:10:33,341 --> 00:10:34,342
Huh?

131
00:10:34,884 --> 00:10:37,219
This was the last bowl of <i>ramyeon.</i>

132
00:10:37,303 --> 00:10:40,097
We spend a third of our budget
just on wasted <i>ramyeon.</i>

133
00:10:40,723 --> 00:10:43,893
Then I'll make a donation
to the budget for you, Tae-gyeong.

134
00:10:45,061 --> 00:10:48,814
Oh, no surprise there. Nice.

135
00:10:59,533 --> 00:11:01,661
Mmm! I'm starting to wake up now.

136
00:11:04,997 --> 00:11:06,624
I bet Dr. Gye's okay, though.

137
00:11:06,707 --> 00:11:08,626
She's not an idiot like me.
That's for sure.

138
00:11:11,087 --> 00:11:12,296
PATIENT (X)
DUMMY

139
00:11:12,380 --> 00:11:13,923
Oh, wow. Ow!

140
00:11:14,006 --> 00:11:15,257
ASSAILANT

141
00:11:15,341 --> 00:11:16,467
Wow, it really hurts.

142
00:11:16,967 --> 00:11:18,010
I think it's broken.

143
00:11:22,348 --> 00:11:23,265
Didn't you see the notice?

144
00:11:23,349 --> 00:11:24,934
It was in the group chat too.

145
00:11:25,017 --> 00:11:27,728
I even posted the training script
outlining the protocol to follow

146
00:11:27,812 --> 00:11:29,230
in case of violence in the ER.

147
00:11:30,189 --> 00:11:31,023
I get it.

148
00:11:31,691 --> 00:11:33,526
You missed it,
which is why you reacted that way.

149
00:11:33,609 --> 00:11:36,112
- You're a real troublemaker.
- Whoa.

150
00:11:36,696 --> 00:11:39,073
How can someone so violent
come into the emergency room…

151
00:11:40,741 --> 00:11:42,159
and save lives the way you do?

152
00:11:42,743 --> 00:11:44,704
They're gonna keep you here, aren't they?

153
00:11:44,787 --> 00:11:46,414
Thank goodness for that.

154
00:11:46,497 --> 00:11:50,209
It's just that we shouldn't be
where they send doctors for punishment.

155
00:11:50,292 --> 00:11:53,045
Why would they do that?
Do they look down on us or what?

156
00:11:54,714 --> 00:11:57,508
Still, it's not so bad down here, huh?

157
00:11:58,342 --> 00:11:59,343
Wow.

158
00:11:59,844 --> 00:12:00,761
Wow! Wow!

159
00:12:00,845 --> 00:12:03,723
Dr. Gye, your hands are so fast! Amazing!

160
00:12:05,474 --> 00:12:07,727
Actually, we haven't cast
the assailant yet,

161
00:12:07,810 --> 00:12:08,853
which is why I was doing it.

162
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:11,480
They're going to shoot
a promo for the hospital.

163
00:12:11,564 --> 00:12:13,691
And the press will be there as well,
and I thought that you might--

164
00:12:13,774 --> 00:12:14,775
That's not something I do.

165
00:12:15,276 --> 00:12:17,820
Your part would be
to just lie quietly in Bed 7

166
00:12:17,903 --> 00:12:19,280
to avoid any trouble.

167
00:12:19,363 --> 00:12:22,158
Well, okay.
You need to rehearse beforehand.

168
00:12:22,241 --> 00:12:24,535
So if there's an incident,
you can respond quickly.

169
00:12:24,618 --> 00:12:26,996
And you haven't even heard the best yet.
Want me to tell you?

170
00:12:27,079 --> 00:12:28,205
Not really. Why would I?

171
00:12:29,498 --> 00:12:31,333
The best part is that I am the director.

172
00:12:31,917 --> 00:12:34,503
I played Macduff
in the 95th production of <i>Macbeth</i>

173
00:12:34,587 --> 00:12:37,339
as a member of Guseo University's
Dramatic Art Society!

174
00:12:37,423 --> 00:12:40,259
- The dramatic what?
- It's a theater club.

175
00:12:40,342 --> 00:12:42,803
- What'd you call me for?
- Bravo!

176
00:12:44,346 --> 00:12:46,932
You've just been cast
as the hostage. Congratulations. Bravo!

177
00:12:47,016 --> 00:12:47,850
What?

178
00:12:47,933 --> 00:12:51,020
Dr. Jo, only you can convey the delicate,
fragile quality of the hostage

179
00:12:51,103 --> 00:12:52,730
along with the tragedy of the moment,

180
00:12:52,813 --> 00:12:54,315
and still truly express--

181
00:12:54,398 --> 00:12:56,650
She's not the type
that would be taken hostage.

182
00:12:56,734 --> 00:12:57,818
Shh.

183
00:12:58,778 --> 00:13:00,571
- I'm leaving. I need to go.
- No, don't. Please.

184
00:13:00,654 --> 00:13:02,823
You're the only one in the hospital
who's got that vibe.

185
00:13:02,907 --> 00:13:04,450
Dr. Kim Seong-jin?

186
00:13:04,533 --> 00:13:07,119
Dr. Cha wants you to check your email.

187
00:13:07,203 --> 00:13:08,662
Oh!

188
00:13:09,413 --> 00:13:10,456
Check your email.

189
00:13:11,707 --> 00:13:14,084
What's wrong with you?
How many days have you gone without sleep?

190
00:13:14,168 --> 00:13:16,796
Is this what they call street casting?

191
00:13:16,879 --> 00:13:20,966
Uh, it's been three or four days?
Although, earlier I slept a little bit.

192
00:13:21,050 --> 00:13:22,134
No, don't sleep at all!

193
00:13:22,218 --> 00:13:24,553
You're young. Half a day of sleep
and you'll be as good as new,

194
00:13:24,637 --> 00:13:25,721
then you'll lose the look.

195
00:13:25,805 --> 00:13:27,431
I have no idea what you're talking about.

196
00:13:27,515 --> 00:13:28,349
Okay, okay, okay.

197
00:13:28,432 --> 00:13:30,810
Why don't we go over there
and practice a few lines?

198
00:13:30,893 --> 00:13:32,228
Hi there, Dr. Jo.

199
00:13:32,311 --> 00:13:34,063
Dr. Gye, I have a lot to tell you.

200
00:13:35,022 --> 00:13:37,107
Dr. Kim seems much better than usual.

201
00:13:37,191 --> 00:13:39,068
That's him doing better?

202
00:13:39,151 --> 00:13:40,569
He probably needs a brain scan.

203
00:13:41,153 --> 00:13:44,698
We usually refer
to that type of behavior as "excitement."

204
00:13:45,783 --> 00:13:49,912
If it's called <i>Macbeth</i>, that means
the main character must be Macbeth.

205
00:13:50,788 --> 00:13:51,956
Macduff…

206
00:13:53,415 --> 00:13:54,708
I wonder if they're related.

207
00:13:54,792 --> 00:13:55,793
Are you…

208
00:13:56,877 --> 00:13:58,796
serious right now?

209
00:13:58,879 --> 00:14:01,841
Oh, so you think all Macs
are related, huh?

210
00:14:02,716 --> 00:14:05,511
Then you must think the hamburger place
was founded by their--

211
00:14:05,594 --> 00:14:07,721
What? I never thought about that.

212
00:14:10,599 --> 00:14:11,725
You're a genius.

213
00:14:11,809 --> 00:14:14,937
You sure can drag me down
to your level quickly. It's annoying.

214
00:14:16,063 --> 00:14:19,400
It has been so quiet in the ER.
Why don't you go home early today--

215
00:14:19,483 --> 00:14:21,569
I wish you hadn't said that.

216
00:14:24,613 --> 00:14:26,532
- Trauma patient.
- What happened?

217
00:14:26,615 --> 00:14:28,033
Five workers fell from the third floor

218
00:14:28,117 --> 00:14:30,119
after a construction site
retaining wall collapsed.

219
00:14:30,202 --> 00:14:31,328
They all fell onto a tree.

220
00:14:31,412 --> 00:14:33,873
Four of them are conscious.
This guy's the only one who isn't.

221
00:14:34,582 --> 00:14:36,500
And his blood pressure keeps dropping.

222
00:14:36,584 --> 00:14:38,043
Get a CT first. Notify the OR.

223
00:14:38,127 --> 00:14:39,211
Okay, will do.

224
00:14:42,298 --> 00:14:44,633
- Is he from the construction site?
- Yeah, he is.

225
00:14:44,717 --> 00:14:45,551
Hang in there.

226
00:14:54,476 --> 00:14:56,437
The ground beneath me just crumbled away.

227
00:14:56,520 --> 00:14:58,147
I was a Marine, so I'm quick.

228
00:14:58,230 --> 00:15:00,816
I grabbed onto whatever
I could see and just--

229
00:15:18,959 --> 00:15:20,794
Whoa!

230
00:15:21,503 --> 00:15:24,298
Well, you did it again, huh?

231
00:15:24,381 --> 00:15:27,176
That was quick. Wasn't it? Right?

232
00:15:27,968 --> 00:15:30,054
You've really got a knack for the ER, huh?

233
00:15:30,137 --> 00:15:33,223
A knack for the ER. You're a game-changer.
That's what you are.

234
00:15:35,225 --> 00:15:37,144
Now, let me just relax
for a minute then--

235
00:15:37,770 --> 00:15:38,604
Huh?

236
00:15:39,063 --> 00:15:40,564
What's wrong? Where are you going?

237
00:15:40,648 --> 00:15:42,608
Dr. Gye? Dr. Gye?

238
00:15:43,233 --> 00:15:44,443
A real game-changer!

239
00:15:44,526 --> 00:15:45,402
HAN JI-HUN, 42 Y/O, M

240
00:15:47,738 --> 00:15:49,615
The CT shows that the liver's bleeding.

241
00:15:49,698 --> 00:15:52,076
Looks like we'll have to scoop it out.

242
00:15:53,619 --> 00:15:54,995
- The blood…
- Hey! Let's go!

243
00:15:55,996 --> 00:15:57,873
Uh, right.

244
00:15:57,957 --> 00:16:00,626
There's so much blood. It's…

245
00:16:01,794 --> 00:16:05,214
- Oh, Dr. Gye Su-jeong.
- What? What's she doing here?

246
00:16:07,216 --> 00:16:08,676
How many units of RBCs do we have?

247
00:16:08,759 --> 00:16:10,344
- Come on. Hurry up.
- Oh, okay.

248
00:16:11,512 --> 00:16:12,596
I mean, this…

249
00:16:13,263 --> 00:16:14,974
Uh, this…

250
00:16:15,057 --> 00:16:17,685
- Hey! What's the problem? Get it together.
- Uh, I'm sorry.

251
00:16:20,854 --> 00:16:22,481
Uh, oh, Dr. Gye.

252
00:16:22,564 --> 00:16:24,566
What are you doing?
This isn't your patient.

253
00:16:24,650 --> 00:16:25,776
Go back to the ER.

254
00:16:28,696 --> 00:16:30,614
What the hell's going on? Seriously!

255
00:16:42,334 --> 00:16:44,920
- Whoa, whoa, whoa, Dr. Gye.
- What? Hey.

256
00:16:54,304 --> 00:16:55,556
BP is stabilizing.

257
00:16:55,639 --> 00:16:58,267
The bleeding is under control.

258
00:17:02,021 --> 00:17:03,397
So now…

259
00:17:06,316 --> 00:17:07,526
Hmm.

260
00:17:09,445 --> 00:17:11,196
Mm-hmm.

261
00:17:17,327 --> 00:17:18,787
Just like I thought.

262
00:17:21,123 --> 00:17:22,041
I found it.

263
00:17:34,011 --> 00:17:35,387
If you found it, suture it.

264
00:17:44,772 --> 00:17:45,814
Suturing.

265
00:17:45,898 --> 00:17:47,941
- Suction.
- Oh, uh…

266
00:17:49,943 --> 00:17:51,653
Prepare 5-0 Prolene.

267
00:17:54,323 --> 00:17:56,241
Director Bu, you never struck me as…

268
00:17:56,909 --> 00:17:58,327
such an impetuous person.

269
00:17:59,286 --> 00:18:01,121
We were just trying to save the hospital.

270
00:18:01,205 --> 00:18:02,623
We didn't mean anything by it.

271
00:18:03,290 --> 00:18:05,876
If our hospital gets on
the public's bad side again…

272
00:18:06,418 --> 00:18:08,629
And what about our bad side?
Doesn't that concern you?

273
00:18:08,712 --> 00:18:11,673
Oh, we wouldn't dare do that.
Not that we're not concerned.

274
00:18:11,757 --> 00:18:13,383
We'd just never even consider it.

275
00:18:13,467 --> 00:18:16,678
If we'd known, we'd never have done it.
We were just impulsive.

276
00:18:16,762 --> 00:18:17,888
It was the former director's blunder?

277
00:18:18,847 --> 00:18:20,349
Cooperate with the appeal?
What the hell is that?

278
00:18:21,725 --> 00:18:24,728
How could you set such a precedent?
This affects every hospital out there.

279
00:18:25,354 --> 00:18:26,480
You're right.

280
00:18:27,689 --> 00:18:28,774
Yes, you're right.

281
00:18:28,857 --> 00:18:32,194
Those hospitals can do
the same thing we did then.

282
00:18:34,571 --> 00:18:35,614
What?

283
00:18:35,697 --> 00:18:39,326
If we had heard them out from the start
and welcomed their investigators

284
00:18:39,409 --> 00:18:41,203
and cooperated with them,

285
00:18:41,286 --> 00:18:45,124
or even simply offered our condolences
to the family of the victim,

286
00:18:46,500 --> 00:18:48,210
do you think it would have come to this?

287
00:18:48,293 --> 00:18:51,004
Apologies, Chairman.
We didn't mean to offend.

288
00:18:51,088 --> 00:18:53,757
And I assure you, we will go apologize
to the members of Magnolia.

289
00:18:59,721 --> 00:19:00,556
Now is the time

290
00:19:01,890 --> 00:19:05,269
for all of us doctors to come together
and unite, and you people

291
00:19:05,352 --> 00:19:06,895
go out there and pull that stunt?

292
00:19:06,979 --> 00:19:09,356
I'm cutting off all support
to this hospital as of now!

293
00:19:09,439 --> 00:19:12,526
You know the hospital
is struggling just to make ends meet.

294
00:19:12,609 --> 00:19:14,236
We had to do it to survive.

295
00:19:14,319 --> 00:19:16,530
We're barely managing to keep
our doors open,

296
00:19:16,613 --> 00:19:18,949
thanks to your support
and coordination, Chairman.

297
00:19:23,036 --> 00:19:24,454
Won't you please reconsider?

298
00:19:26,373 --> 00:19:29,543
Well, you made such a stink
about being short-staffed and all,

299
00:19:29,626 --> 00:19:32,421
so I sent you a carefully selected
and very talented doctor.

300
00:19:33,005 --> 00:19:34,798
And you didn't even thank me.

301
00:19:35,924 --> 00:19:37,926
So, how do you like Dr. Na?
He's good, isn't he?

302
00:19:38,010 --> 00:19:40,637
Oh! He's truly amazing.

303
00:19:41,138 --> 00:19:44,808
So skilled as a doctor,
and also a really good guy.

304
00:19:44,892 --> 00:19:48,520
He seems all right so far,
but it's a little early to tell for sure.

305
00:19:51,106 --> 00:19:52,524
I'm very grateful, though.

306
00:19:55,360 --> 00:19:58,322
The mayor and I will be dropping by
here soon, so get ready for that.

307
00:19:58,405 --> 00:19:59,907
And the purpose of your visit?

308
00:19:59,990 --> 00:20:01,658
Oh, of course, he should come.

309
00:20:01,742 --> 00:20:04,286
After all, we're the region's
most important hospital.

310
00:20:04,369 --> 00:20:06,246
What should we do to prepare for you?

311
00:20:06,872 --> 00:20:09,249
You should know the drill by now.

312
00:20:09,333 --> 00:20:12,336
Oh, there was no children's
hospital back when the mayor worked here.

313
00:20:12,419 --> 00:20:15,088
- So it might be a good idea to do a tour?
- That sounds good.

314
00:20:15,172 --> 00:20:16,006
Great.

315
00:20:17,257 --> 00:20:18,926
Everyone is struggling these days.

316
00:20:19,509 --> 00:20:22,346
You think we're giving you money
because we've got too much lying around?

317
00:20:22,429 --> 00:20:23,889
We'll do our best.

318
00:20:23,972 --> 00:20:26,350
Do our best, my ass.

319
00:20:26,433 --> 00:20:27,768
TIME TO ADMINISTER EYE DROPS

320
00:20:30,562 --> 00:20:32,439
Oh. Thank you for your hard work.

321
00:20:32,522 --> 00:20:34,608
No worries. It was pretty routine.

322
00:20:34,691 --> 00:20:38,111
And that doctor, Snake Su-jeong,
did the important part.

323
00:20:38,195 --> 00:20:39,446
Oh…

324
00:20:40,322 --> 00:20:42,241
Just kidding.

325
00:20:42,324 --> 00:20:43,158
Everyone calls her that,

326
00:20:43,242 --> 00:20:47,412
- so I thought I'd give it a whirl.
- Oh. Oh, you must have been offended.

327
00:20:47,496 --> 00:20:49,665
She didn't mean to intrude
during your surgery.

328
00:20:49,748 --> 00:20:51,875
Sometimes she just leaps before she looks.

329
00:20:51,959 --> 00:20:55,796
Hmm, you're the only one who talks about
Dr. Gye with any real decency.

330
00:20:56,380 --> 00:20:57,881
Oh, is that so?

331
00:20:59,258 --> 00:21:02,052
- I guess they are pretty disrespectful.
- Oh?

332
00:21:03,387 --> 00:21:04,471
Your face just dropped.

333
00:21:05,305 --> 00:21:06,139
Are you guys close?

334
00:21:06,223 --> 00:21:07,849
Huh? Oh, no.

335
00:21:08,809 --> 00:21:13,146
Uh, it wouldn't be accurate
to describe us as close.

336
00:21:13,730 --> 00:21:14,690
I better get going.

337
00:21:16,566 --> 00:21:17,985
I'd like to use that word.

338
00:21:19,403 --> 00:21:20,779
"Close," I mean.

339
00:21:22,030 --> 00:21:23,115
In regard to…

340
00:21:24,700 --> 00:21:25,909
Dr. Gye and me.

341
00:21:27,661 --> 00:21:29,037
I hope you could
help me out with that.

342
00:21:44,219 --> 00:21:46,763
Why would you march
into someone else's OR like that, huh?

343
00:21:50,058 --> 00:21:53,103
Do you think Ms. Jang Hui-suk from
the temp agency has heard about it yet?

344
00:21:54,062 --> 00:21:54,896
Oh, shit.

345
00:21:56,523 --> 00:21:59,151
People are talking about it
differently this time.

346
00:21:59,234 --> 00:22:00,277
It was no big deal.

347
00:22:00,360 --> 00:22:02,738
The surgery was successful
and the patient is okay.

348
00:22:03,989 --> 00:22:06,116
Anything interesting
concerning Dr. Na Dae-il?

349
00:22:06,199 --> 00:22:07,409
We didn't get into a fight.

350
00:22:07,492 --> 00:22:10,454
Bingo! There you go.
That's not logical, is it?

351
00:22:10,537 --> 00:22:11,997
You barge into his OR,

352
00:22:12,080 --> 00:22:14,624
he's supposed to throw scissors
at the wall or swear up and down at you,

353
00:22:14,708 --> 00:22:16,293
make a scene and kick you out.

354
00:22:16,376 --> 00:22:19,588
It's that he smiled. Who does that?
Crazy, isn't it?

355
00:22:19,671 --> 00:22:21,173
Is it that crazy?

356
00:22:21,256 --> 00:22:23,300
Uh…

357
00:22:23,383 --> 00:22:26,094
There's gotta be soundproof carpet
in front of the ER desk.

358
00:22:26,178 --> 00:22:28,263
Everyone keeps sneaking up on me.

359
00:22:28,347 --> 00:22:31,350
Oh, um, nice to meet you.
You're Dr. Na Dae-il, aren't you?

360
00:22:31,975 --> 00:22:33,101
Pleasure meeting you.

361
00:22:33,185 --> 00:22:34,478
You must be Dr. Kim Seong-jin.

362
00:22:34,561 --> 00:22:35,854
I think so, yeah.

363
00:22:36,646 --> 00:22:39,733
Oh, as the head of the ER,
it's my fault that Dr. Gye here

364
00:22:39,816 --> 00:22:42,527
caused a scene in your OR.
I'm deeply apologetic.

365
00:22:42,611 --> 00:22:45,155
Please go easy on her.

366
00:22:45,238 --> 00:22:47,824
No, please, cause another scene.

367
00:22:47,908 --> 00:22:48,909
Huh?

368
00:22:48,992 --> 00:22:51,870
After seeing the CT scan,
she knew what needed to be done.

369
00:22:51,953 --> 00:22:53,121
And she was right.

370
00:22:54,122 --> 00:22:55,290
Ah…

371
00:22:59,211 --> 00:23:01,088
<i>Dr. Jo, emergency at the ER desk.</i>

372
00:23:01,171 --> 00:23:02,422
<i>Come diagnose the situation here.</i>

373
00:23:03,882 --> 00:23:06,551
But I knew it too.

374
00:23:07,177 --> 00:23:11,181
I just missed my opportunity
due to your dynamic entrance.

375
00:23:18,480 --> 00:23:20,774
Dr. Gye, I know you're busy working,

376
00:23:20,857 --> 00:23:24,194
but why don't you show some appreciation
for what Dr. Na brought?

377
00:23:24,277 --> 00:23:26,446
There's bread too. Oh, wow.

378
00:23:27,489 --> 00:23:29,741
<i>I'm an anesthesiologist.</i>

379
00:23:29,825 --> 00:23:31,535
<i>You're no fun, Won-jin. No fun.</i>

380
00:23:32,369 --> 00:23:36,039
I may not look it,
but my pride isn't easily injured.

381
00:23:37,541 --> 00:23:40,669
But still, it's impressive that you
figured it out as quickly as you did.

382
00:23:49,886 --> 00:23:52,305
Dr. Park Tae-gyeong told me
you liked this kind of stuff.

383
00:23:52,389 --> 00:23:54,141
Is that not true?
Did I buy the wrong thing?

384
00:23:54,224 --> 00:23:56,476
Mmm! No, it's delicious.

385
00:23:56,560 --> 00:23:57,602
Yeah.

386
00:23:58,728 --> 00:24:00,105
Why are you staring?

387
00:24:05,235 --> 00:24:06,194
What are you looking at?

388
00:24:06,278 --> 00:24:08,405
Oh, yeah, you're standing
where she always looks.

389
00:24:08,488 --> 00:24:09,489
Sorry?

390
00:24:10,157 --> 00:24:11,658
- I'll be going no.
- Yeah. See you.

391
00:24:13,118 --> 00:24:14,870
Where is Dr. Gye Su-jeong going?

392
00:24:15,370 --> 00:24:16,371
Oh, home. She's clocking out.

393
00:24:19,124 --> 00:24:20,000
Ah, right.

394
00:24:21,835 --> 00:24:23,295
That's right. Mm-hmm.

395
00:24:23,378 --> 00:24:24,588
Right on time.

396
00:24:28,216 --> 00:24:29,217
Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

397
00:24:29,301 --> 00:24:32,888
RECOVERY ROOM

398
00:24:44,858 --> 00:24:46,610
Oh, Dr. Na, what brings you here?

399
00:24:49,988 --> 00:24:52,199
Oh, do you want me to call her over here?

400
00:24:52,282 --> 00:24:53,200
No, thank you.

401
00:24:54,534 --> 00:24:56,036
That's the first patient to be listed…

402
00:24:56,119 --> 00:24:56,953
YEO JEONG-SUN

403
00:24:57,037 --> 00:24:59,164
…under Dr. Gye Su-jeong's name.

404
00:24:59,247 --> 00:25:02,876
Oh! This is the craniotomy she did.
Is that true?

405
00:25:02,959 --> 00:25:04,085
Mm-hmm, yeah.

406
00:25:04,169 --> 00:25:07,339
It's not actually the first surgery
she did. It's just the first one--

407
00:25:07,422 --> 00:25:08,548
I heard she was fast.

408
00:25:09,674 --> 00:25:11,676
- Yeah.
- How fast?

409
00:25:11,760 --> 00:25:14,137
Fast enough that no one
really wants to talk about it much.

410
00:25:16,181 --> 00:25:17,015
Really?

411
00:25:17,641 --> 00:25:21,478
Last time, they switched surgeons
from Dr. Do to Dr. Gye,

412
00:25:21,561 --> 00:25:24,314
so this patient
isn't really her first, but still.

413
00:25:24,397 --> 00:25:26,191
From the start, she…

414
00:25:28,527 --> 00:25:29,361
What's his deal?

415
00:25:34,324 --> 00:25:36,034
YEO JEONG-SUN
PRIMARY: GYE SU-JEONG

416
00:26:05,313 --> 00:26:07,691
So, you got off work, then what?

417
00:26:07,774 --> 00:26:09,943
What could be more romantic
than two doctors

418
00:26:10,026 --> 00:26:12,279
dipping their hands
into a blood-filled abdomen?

419
00:26:12,362 --> 00:26:13,863
So sweet!

420
00:26:13,947 --> 00:26:15,907
And together, they staunched the bleeding.

421
00:26:15,991 --> 00:26:17,951
Oh, they should have done
the ligation together too.

422
00:26:18,034 --> 00:26:19,703
- Can we play?
- He didn't follow you?

423
00:26:19,786 --> 00:26:21,496
Yeah, did he chase after you?

424
00:26:23,081 --> 00:26:23,915
Who?

425
00:26:23,999 --> 00:26:25,750
- Come on, you know who.
- Are you serious?

426
00:26:25,834 --> 00:26:28,211
- Hey, you're a moron. You're such a moron.
- You really are a silly kid.

427
00:26:28,295 --> 00:26:30,297
- Completely silly.
- You know if this guy was in the military,

428
00:26:30,380 --> 00:26:33,341
then he's got to be
a pretty decent, upstanding person.

429
00:26:33,425 --> 00:26:34,718
You know, right?

430
00:26:34,801 --> 00:26:36,261
Oh!

431
00:26:36,344 --> 00:26:38,763
- He's stunning. Look at him.
- Whoa!

432
00:26:38,847 --> 00:26:40,098
Whoa!

433
00:26:40,181 --> 00:26:42,601
- Oh, be still my heart!
- He's a pretty boy, huh?

434
00:26:42,684 --> 00:26:44,894
- He got your number, right?
- What number?

435
00:26:44,978 --> 00:26:48,398
Man, you South Koreans need to step it up.
He get your digits, or what?

436
00:26:48,481 --> 00:26:51,401
Wow, so what makes you so cool?

437
00:26:52,110 --> 00:26:54,696
Hey, there's a lot more
where that came from.

438
00:26:55,322 --> 00:26:56,531
"I ate and left no crumbs."

439
00:26:57,490 --> 00:26:59,117
"Never mind. I can't even."

440
00:26:59,200 --> 00:27:00,035
What?

441
00:27:01,077 --> 00:27:02,787
That guy's hands smell fishy.

442
00:27:04,289 --> 00:27:05,790
The smell is way too familiar.

443
00:27:07,250 --> 00:27:09,628
"Let's shut our traps and give it a go."

444
00:27:09,711 --> 00:27:11,504
- What's that?
- I said, "Shut--"

445
00:27:13,006 --> 00:27:14,382
I heard the patient lived.

446
00:27:15,383 --> 00:27:17,260
You said the hospital didn't call you.

447
00:27:17,344 --> 00:27:19,554
Come on. Is there anything
she doesn't know?

448
00:27:19,679 --> 00:27:21,931
Inside the hospital, Ms. Jang knows all.

449
00:27:22,015 --> 00:27:23,058
Crap.

450
00:27:24,100 --> 00:27:26,353
He smells fishy? And not like money?

451
00:27:27,020 --> 00:27:28,521
Well, money smells fishy.

452
00:27:29,731 --> 00:27:31,983
No! Ugh.

453
00:27:40,241 --> 00:27:43,912
Oh, no. This is Dr. Ma's book.
He's gonna kill me.

454
00:27:58,551 --> 00:28:00,637
<i>But as an intern,</i>
<i>just quietly finish your month with us</i>

455
00:28:00,720 --> 00:28:01,554
<i>and then go on your way.</i>

456
00:28:01,638 --> 00:28:03,515
I really don't want to see
any more interns

457
00:28:03,598 --> 00:28:05,433
doing a rotation in surgery
pretending to be doctors

458
00:28:05,517 --> 00:28:07,143
with some great sense of duty only to…

459
00:28:08,144 --> 00:28:09,854
<i>go to an easier department somewhere.</i>

460
00:28:10,438 --> 00:28:12,023
<i>You won't be a surgeon anyway.</i>

461
00:28:16,152 --> 00:28:17,737
This damn blood…

462
00:28:17,821 --> 00:28:19,531
I'm sick of it already.

463
00:28:20,281 --> 00:28:22,325
And I want to be a doctor. How pathetic.

464
00:28:24,202 --> 00:28:25,662
God.

465
00:28:29,124 --> 00:28:31,126
YEO JEONG-SUN

466
00:28:44,389 --> 00:28:45,640
She's using that already?

467
00:28:48,852 --> 00:28:49,769
She's amazing.

468
00:29:02,365 --> 00:29:05,702
It's time to go to school.

469
00:29:09,330 --> 00:29:10,331
Oh.

470
00:29:11,249 --> 00:29:12,625
Hey, have a…

471
00:29:12,709 --> 00:29:14,461
Have a good day! See you--

472
00:29:22,719 --> 00:29:23,845
ANTACIDS

473
00:29:30,852 --> 00:29:32,729
DESTINATION:
GUSEO UNIVERSITY SEONAM MEDICAL CENTER

474
00:29:37,776 --> 00:29:39,027
Dr. Gye Su-Jeong!

475
00:29:44,115 --> 00:29:46,701
I want to finish what I was saying
yesterday in the elevator.

476
00:29:49,287 --> 00:29:52,040
Okay.

477
00:30:02,217 --> 00:30:05,220
The operation was completed incorrectly.
When that rupture happens,

478
00:30:05,303 --> 00:30:06,721
it'll be on your watch.

479
00:30:06,805 --> 00:30:08,640
If not, then I'll hand
my white coat to you.

480
00:30:08,723 --> 00:30:10,099
Yeah, sure, I'll throw mine in too.

481
00:30:10,183 --> 00:30:12,477
Let's hope he's wrong,
and I know he's not. You better be sure.

482
00:30:12,560 --> 00:30:16,105
Min-gu, you threatening my career
doesn't scare me at all.

483
00:30:18,191 --> 00:30:19,400
Polish your resumes.

484
00:30:53,393 --> 00:30:55,812
They moved the patient
to the general ward,

485
00:30:55,895 --> 00:30:57,897
which means the aneurysm didn't rupture.

486
00:31:33,016 --> 00:31:33,975
<i>See you later.</i>

487
00:31:35,435 --> 00:31:38,855
BUIL DINER

488
00:31:38,938 --> 00:31:40,607
Oh! We'll get the next open table.

489
00:31:40,690 --> 00:31:45,570
We've been waiting 20 minutes already.
I hate waiting in line to eat like this.

490
00:31:45,653 --> 00:31:47,280
Why'd you drag me out here anyway?

491
00:31:47,363 --> 00:31:49,699
Relax, enjoy the nice weather.

492
00:31:49,782 --> 00:31:53,411
This is my way of welcoming
Dr. Gye to the ER department.

493
00:31:53,494 --> 00:31:55,246
Then you should have eaten
with the ER team.

494
00:31:55,330 --> 00:31:56,456
Why'd you ask Dr. Park and me?

495
00:31:56,539 --> 00:31:59,334
Well, I mean, we're always so busy,
we have to take turns eating.

496
00:31:59,417 --> 00:32:02,921
And I thought that it would be nice
to eat together for a change.

497
00:32:03,004 --> 00:32:05,757
So I begged another doctor to cover us
so we could all go out.

498
00:32:06,424 --> 00:32:07,759
Ah! Ah!

499
00:32:07,842 --> 00:32:11,638
I-- I heard about that run-in you had,
you know, what happened in the elevator.

500
00:32:11,721 --> 00:32:13,890
You know? You know this?

501
00:32:13,973 --> 00:32:15,183
I felt a little, you know.

502
00:32:15,266 --> 00:32:18,394
And you two helped get
Dr. Gye into the ER,

503
00:32:18,478 --> 00:32:20,313
so I thought I might as well
invite you guys also.

504
00:32:21,230 --> 00:32:23,691
Well, I guess I can't argue with that.

505
00:32:24,817 --> 00:32:27,862
Whoa, whoa, whoa!
You're not backing out now, are you?

506
00:32:27,946 --> 00:32:29,197
Stick it out. Just wait a sec.

507
00:32:30,156 --> 00:32:32,867
The only reason I came
is 'cause you're buying.

508
00:32:32,951 --> 00:32:35,036
Wait, you're buying?

509
00:32:35,119 --> 00:32:38,456
Dr. Gye is my one-woman army.
It's the least I could do.

510
00:32:38,539 --> 00:32:41,209
Why don't you cut ties
with those damn surgeons

511
00:32:41,292 --> 00:32:42,752
and keep working in the ER with me?

512
00:32:44,671 --> 00:32:47,465
What's his deal?
He seems like a pretty hard worker, huh?

513
00:32:47,548 --> 00:32:50,843
But he always looks so weak and frail.

514
00:32:50,927 --> 00:32:52,053
He needs herbal medicine.

515
00:32:52,136 --> 00:32:54,305
Says a Western medicine practitioner.

516
00:32:54,389 --> 00:32:56,599
Come on, we all know that, as kids,

517
00:32:56,683 --> 00:32:58,851
our grandmothers' cures
were nothing short of miraculous.

518
00:32:58,935 --> 00:33:01,729
It's taking so long because
we're waiting for a table for four.

519
00:33:01,813 --> 00:33:03,022
We should sit two per table.

520
00:33:03,106 --> 00:33:04,774
What are you talking about?

521
00:33:04,857 --> 00:33:06,609
Look, the point was to eat together.

522
00:33:06,693 --> 00:33:08,611
It defeats the purpose
if we sit separately.

523
00:33:08,695 --> 00:33:10,655
Yeah, but if someone comes out alone,

524
00:33:10,738 --> 00:33:12,031
I'll take their table.

525
00:33:12,782 --> 00:33:15,034
It's actually nice
sitting outside like this.

526
00:33:15,118 --> 00:33:17,036
I'm always in the hospital at this hour.

527
00:33:19,080 --> 00:33:20,665
Oh! There's a table. Let's go!

528
00:33:20,748 --> 00:33:22,542
There's a table! Let's go!
There's a table now!

529
00:33:26,212 --> 00:33:27,964
Are you okay?

530
00:33:28,047 --> 00:33:29,799
- What's the matter?
- Mr. Kwon?

531
00:33:31,843 --> 00:33:32,844
He's not picking up.

532
00:33:32,927 --> 00:33:34,387
KWON CHUNG-HYEON
UGANG PHARMACEUTICALS

533
00:33:34,470 --> 00:33:35,847
That's not like him at all.

534
00:33:35,930 --> 00:33:39,267
I know, right? He always calls
if he's late, even five minutes.

535
00:33:39,350 --> 00:33:40,810
Maybe he's passed out somewhere.

536
00:33:40,893 --> 00:33:43,146
Sometimes pharmaceutical reps
are so hungover

537
00:33:43,229 --> 00:33:44,856
from drinking with clients all night

538
00:33:44,939 --> 00:33:46,858
that they sleep it off in their cars.

539
00:33:46,941 --> 00:33:48,026
Uh, not Mr. Kwon.

540
00:33:48,693 --> 00:33:50,778
One time, there was a seminar
in the province.

541
00:33:50,862 --> 00:33:52,071
Mmm! Mm-hmm!

542
00:33:52,155 --> 00:33:55,950
Afterward, he treated us to a round of
golf, 18 holes, and an expensive dinner.

543
00:33:56,034 --> 00:33:58,161
And at the bar, we mixed liquor and beer.

544
00:33:58,244 --> 00:34:00,246
Oh, Mr. Kwon's liquor-and-beer mix
is so good!

545
00:34:02,957 --> 00:34:05,376
Do Yun-sik!

546
00:34:07,879 --> 00:34:09,547
I'm rooting for us!

547
00:34:12,550 --> 00:34:14,719
Hey, Mr. Kwon, over here.

548
00:34:14,802 --> 00:34:18,973
<i>I am that person</i>
<i>No matter what anyone says </i>

549
00:34:19,057 --> 00:34:21,184
- Yeah!
- <i>No matter what anyone says </i>

550
00:34:21,267 --> 00:34:24,187
<i>More beautiful than… </i>

551
00:34:24,270 --> 00:34:28,357
- <i>No matter what anyone says</i>
- <i>No matter what anyone says </i>

552
00:34:28,441 --> 00:34:31,611
<i>Chung-hyeon is more beautiful</i>
<i>Than a flower </i>

553
00:34:31,694 --> 00:34:33,112
Okay.

554
00:34:33,905 --> 00:34:35,823
Okay. We're almost there.

555
00:34:35,907 --> 00:34:37,492
Okay, okay.

556
00:34:37,575 --> 00:34:39,327
Okay, okay…

557
00:34:41,621 --> 00:34:43,331
Here you go. Now I'll let you rest.

558
00:34:43,414 --> 00:34:44,665
- Bye!
- Good night.

559
00:34:45,666 --> 00:34:47,168
<i>He slept at the bathhouse</i>

560
00:34:47,251 --> 00:34:50,546
and was waiting for us in the lobby
the next morning to buy us hangover soup.

561
00:34:50,630 --> 00:34:52,882
He even drove us
all the way back to Seoul.

562
00:34:52,965 --> 00:34:55,093
His liver? I don't know.
It's extraordinary.

563
00:34:55,176 --> 00:34:58,805
Oh, remember the last team dinner?
Mr. Kwon paid for everything.

564
00:34:58,888 --> 00:35:02,100
Even down to the designated drivers.
He took care of all of it.

565
00:35:02,183 --> 00:35:06,646
As far as these pharmaceutical reps
are concerned, let's show some restraint.

566
00:35:12,318 --> 00:35:15,571
Oh, it's just that it's
a long-standing tradition.

567
00:35:15,655 --> 00:35:19,408
At one point, there were whispers
about you asking a pharmaceutical employee

568
00:35:20,910 --> 00:35:22,537
to help with a paper you were working on.

569
00:35:23,329 --> 00:35:27,166
That was because it was a research paper
funded by that pharmaceutical company.

570
00:35:27,250 --> 00:35:28,751
But why were there whispers?

571
00:35:30,795 --> 00:35:32,672
Rumors of kickbacks.

572
00:35:32,755 --> 00:35:34,340
I'm sorry. I'll be more careful.

573
00:35:35,675 --> 00:35:36,759
Let's make sure

574
00:35:37,552 --> 00:35:39,387
that word is never heard in this hospital.

575
00:35:43,307 --> 00:35:45,768
Let's sit here.

576
00:35:47,645 --> 00:35:48,896
Dr. Mun Yeong-jong.

577
00:35:50,731 --> 00:35:52,024
Have you been drinking this morning?

578
00:35:54,193 --> 00:35:55,570
What are you talking about?

579
00:35:56,154 --> 00:35:59,407
- He has been.
- Oh, yesterday I did.

580
00:35:59,490 --> 00:36:00,700
Can you still smell it?

581
00:36:01,742 --> 00:36:04,954
- I should drink a hangover cure.
- Last night you were working.

582
00:36:06,998 --> 00:36:10,710
I mean, it's not like it's ever affected
any of my surgeries.

583
00:36:10,793 --> 00:36:12,753
You could face disciplinary action.

584
00:36:12,837 --> 00:36:13,880
Oh, is that right?

585
00:36:17,133 --> 00:36:18,801
Now, you listen here, Director--

586
00:36:18,885 --> 00:36:21,387
Oh, Dr. Mun, this isn't the place.

587
00:36:24,140 --> 00:36:25,308
Enjoy your meal.

588
00:36:25,391 --> 00:36:27,476
- Good day. Good day.
- Yeah, yeah, enjoy.

589
00:36:28,269 --> 00:36:30,188
Well, it's about time, Mr. Kwon--

590
00:36:31,230 --> 00:36:32,148
Hello?

591
00:36:33,399 --> 00:36:34,317
What?

592
00:36:34,400 --> 00:36:35,651
Well, who are you?

593
00:36:38,654 --> 00:36:39,530
Gye Su-jeong?

594
00:36:41,908 --> 00:36:43,326
You need surgery right now.

595
00:36:43,409 --> 00:36:46,495
- Well, I feel fine now, but thanks.
- That's how cholecystitis is.

596
00:36:46,579 --> 00:36:48,956
Over time, the pain will always come back.

597
00:36:49,665 --> 00:36:51,542
How about next week? Is that okay?

598
00:36:51,626 --> 00:36:53,252
- This week is very--
- Mr. Kwon.

599
00:36:53,336 --> 00:36:55,004
You're familiar
with the healthcare industry,

600
00:36:55,087 --> 00:36:57,131
so why are you putting off
treatment of your illness?

601
00:36:57,715 --> 00:36:59,967
Every single doctor
in this hospital knows you.

602
00:37:00,051 --> 00:37:02,136
- I don't know him.
- Now you do.

603
00:37:02,220 --> 00:37:04,847
Dr. Gye, thank you for helping me.
I was lucky you were there. Thank you.

604
00:37:06,474 --> 00:37:08,684
Why'd he get so mad
when he's the one who called?

605
00:37:08,768 --> 00:37:09,769
Who was mad?

606
00:37:11,979 --> 00:37:12,813
Dr. Do called me.

607
00:37:12,897 --> 00:37:14,774
Ah, the bush league surgeon.

608
00:37:14,857 --> 00:37:17,568
Um, did you tell Dr. Do
that I was here, by any chance?

609
00:37:18,527 --> 00:37:20,738
- Ah!
- No, don't get up.

610
00:37:22,156 --> 00:37:23,157
Uh, did you--

611
00:37:25,284 --> 00:37:27,745
- Did you schedule the surgery?
- I'm gonna do it next week.

612
00:37:27,828 --> 00:37:29,288
Next week? Why?

613
00:37:29,372 --> 00:37:30,373
This isn't your first episode.

614
00:37:30,957 --> 00:37:33,251
I thought it was just indigestion
or something.

615
00:37:34,669 --> 00:37:36,420
I'm sorry, Dr. Do, but…

616
00:37:37,505 --> 00:37:38,422
I couldn't make our meeting.

617
00:37:38,506 --> 00:37:40,883
Ah, no, come on. You're sick. It's okay.

618
00:37:40,967 --> 00:37:42,760
Put Mr. Kwon's surgery on my schedule.

619
00:37:42,843 --> 00:37:44,303
- Ah, well…
- Mmm!

620
00:37:44,971 --> 00:37:45,805
Oh, hey.

621
00:37:45,888 --> 00:37:47,765
Hello, sir!

622
00:37:51,185 --> 00:37:53,980
I was looking forward to dinner tonight,
but I don't think I can make it.

623
00:37:54,063 --> 00:37:56,065
I just had a look at your ultrasound.

624
00:37:56,691 --> 00:37:58,484
But you've already been diagnosed
and you need surgery.

625
00:37:58,567 --> 00:38:01,654
I know. I was hoping
you could do my surgery.

626
00:38:02,863 --> 00:38:04,740
Uh, I was gonna ask you tonight.

627
00:38:04,824 --> 00:38:06,492
You should have had the surgery earlier.

628
00:38:06,575 --> 00:38:09,328
What were you thinking, Private Kwon?

629
00:38:12,206 --> 00:38:14,458
- Oh, there he goes.
- Whoops!

630
00:38:14,542 --> 00:38:15,876
Take it like a man, you little shit.

631
00:38:15,960 --> 00:38:18,879
- What's the matter?
- Need a hand? Wow.

632
00:38:18,963 --> 00:38:21,090
- Yeah, that's a good job.
- Okay, get ready.

633
00:38:21,173 --> 00:38:22,967
- Focus, focus.
- Go.

634
00:38:23,050 --> 00:38:24,969
Hey, that's good. That's good.

635
00:38:25,052 --> 00:38:27,722
- Hey, no hands.
- Come on, geez!

636
00:38:27,805 --> 00:38:29,640
<i>After my father passed away,</i>

637
00:38:29,724 --> 00:38:32,184
<i>- my family went bankrupt.</i>
- Come on, man!

638
00:38:32,268 --> 00:38:33,769
<i>Since I couldn't do anything to help,</i>

639
00:38:33,853 --> 00:38:37,356
<i>I figured I could at least save the family</i>
<i>money by taking a break from college</i>

640
00:38:37,440 --> 00:38:39,317
<i>and doing my military service.</i>

641
00:38:39,900 --> 00:38:42,028
- All right, here we go.
- Open his mouth, open his mouth.

642
00:38:42,111 --> 00:38:44,155
- Open it, open it.
- Open up!

643
00:38:46,699 --> 00:38:48,326
<i>And that's when the nightmare began.</i>

644
00:38:53,456 --> 00:38:56,667
- <i>I still don't know why…</i>
- Faster, faster.

645
00:38:56,751 --> 00:38:59,879
<i>- …why they bullied me so much.</i>
- Do it like this. Hey! More!

646
00:38:59,962 --> 00:39:01,589
<i>They picked fights with me.</i>

647
00:39:01,672 --> 00:39:05,051
<i>Made me do exercises and beat me up.</i>

648
00:39:05,134 --> 00:39:07,428
Do it right, you dumbass! Geez!

649
00:39:07,511 --> 00:39:08,971
<i>It got worse and worse.</i>

650
00:39:09,055 --> 00:39:11,682
- Spin! Spin!
- <i>Then one night,</i>

651
00:39:11,766 --> 00:39:13,768
<i>I couldn't take it anymore</i>
<i>and I fought back.</i>

652
00:39:14,810 --> 00:39:17,271
<i>- And that was the last straw.</i>
- Bastard.

653
00:39:18,439 --> 00:39:20,941
Here you go!

654
00:39:21,025 --> 00:39:23,152
- Little shit!
- One more!

655
00:39:23,235 --> 00:39:25,613
Like that?

656
00:39:25,696 --> 00:39:27,281
Ah, shit.

657
00:39:29,784 --> 00:39:32,828
You sons of bitches.
What the hell are you doing?

658
00:39:34,246 --> 00:39:36,123
Kwon Chung-hyeon.

659
00:39:36,207 --> 00:39:37,541
Kwon Chung-hyeon.

660
00:39:40,836 --> 00:39:41,670
Private Kwon.

661
00:39:42,254 --> 00:39:44,590
Can you hear me? Private Kwon?

662
00:39:44,673 --> 00:39:46,342
Private Kwon, hang in there.

663
00:39:47,259 --> 00:39:48,761
There's nothing we can do here.

664
00:39:48,844 --> 00:39:50,304
The ambulance will be here soon.

665
00:39:51,472 --> 00:39:54,809
The ambulance is on the way, but it'll
take 30 to 40 minutes to get here.

666
00:39:54,892 --> 00:39:55,726
What?

667
00:40:00,981 --> 00:40:02,191
He's bleeding internally.

668
00:40:03,442 --> 00:40:05,403
At this rate,
he won't make it to the hospital.

669
00:40:08,489 --> 00:40:09,365
Private Kwon.

670
00:40:10,074 --> 00:40:11,325
Private Kwon, can you hear me?

671
00:40:12,034 --> 00:40:12,868
Stay with me!

672
00:40:14,286 --> 00:40:15,871
Hey, Kwon Chung-hyeon, stay with me!

673
00:40:17,706 --> 00:40:18,707
I'm gonna save you.

674
00:40:19,792 --> 00:40:21,001
No matter what, I'll save you.

675
00:40:24,171 --> 00:40:25,631
NAMIL CLINIC

676
00:40:31,220 --> 00:40:34,849
Uh… any other medical staff around?

677
00:40:34,932 --> 00:40:35,850
No.

678
00:40:45,526 --> 00:40:46,485
Kwon Chung-hyeon.

679
00:40:47,069 --> 00:40:48,571
Kwon Chung-hyeon, wake up.

680
00:40:48,654 --> 00:40:51,490
You need to put those guys away.
Open your eyes.

681
00:40:53,284 --> 00:40:54,160
I'll save you.

682
00:40:55,244 --> 00:40:56,454
Hang in there.

683
00:41:00,583 --> 00:41:01,500
I'll do it.

684
00:41:07,006 --> 00:41:09,091
Mr. Kwon used to visit him occasionally,

685
00:41:09,175 --> 00:41:11,260
even after he was discharged
from the military.

686
00:41:11,343 --> 00:41:14,263
- And they always kept in touch.
- I can see why. Wow.

687
00:41:14,346 --> 00:41:16,974
That Na Dae-il, he's awesome.

688
00:41:17,725 --> 00:41:19,393
Mr. Kwon and I were talking one time,

689
00:41:19,477 --> 00:41:21,061
and he casually mentioned

690
00:41:21,145 --> 00:41:23,689
that he owed his life to someone he met
while he was enlisted.

691
00:41:23,772 --> 00:41:25,649
So, I thought he was just tipsy,

692
00:41:26,233 --> 00:41:28,944
but he said that person inspired him
to work in the medical field.

693
00:41:29,028 --> 00:41:30,988
- Hmm.
- So it was true.

694
00:41:31,071 --> 00:41:32,114
Mm-hmm.

695
00:41:32,198 --> 00:41:34,450
Dr. Na testified at the Center
for Military Human Rights.

696
00:41:34,533 --> 00:41:35,868
Ah!

697
00:41:35,951 --> 00:41:39,205
And that Snake Su-jeong,
disrespecting such a heroic doctor.

698
00:41:39,288 --> 00:41:41,790
You saw what she did.
I'm not kidding. It was terrible.

699
00:41:42,374 --> 00:41:44,668
So, how are you going to operate?

700
00:41:45,794 --> 00:41:47,379
<i>"Are you going in laparoscopically?"</i>

701
00:41:47,463 --> 00:41:50,257
Who would cut up a patient
when they could do it laparoscopically?

702
00:41:50,341 --> 00:41:52,718
And yet, last time,
she was the one going on and on

703
00:41:52,801 --> 00:41:54,220
about minimally invasive surgery.

704
00:41:54,303 --> 00:41:58,849
"Recovery from laparoscopic surgery
is quicker. I'll do the best I can."

705
00:41:59,767 --> 00:42:02,353
Did you see how he was beaming?
His face looked like the sun!

706
00:42:04,021 --> 00:42:07,942
And to think, under those conditions, he
did the anesthesia and he did the surgery.

707
00:42:09,193 --> 00:42:10,194
He really is a hero.

708
00:42:11,362 --> 00:42:14,156
If you hadn't gone for the double board
and just done the fellowship,

709
00:42:14,240 --> 00:42:15,991
that would have been your spot, easy.

710
00:42:16,075 --> 00:42:17,243
Yeah.

711
00:42:17,326 --> 00:42:18,786
I don't know about that.

712
00:42:18,869 --> 00:42:21,830
This whole thing is the entire fault
of Snake Su-jeong.

713
00:42:21,914 --> 00:42:24,750
Everyone is all in a tizzy
because of her, you know?

714
00:42:26,752 --> 00:42:27,836
You're not quitting neurosurgery, are you?

715
00:42:31,674 --> 00:42:32,550
Well?

716
00:42:33,342 --> 00:42:34,843
It's a simple question.

717
00:42:36,220 --> 00:42:38,973
You can't quit!
You have to stay with us, man!

718
00:42:40,057 --> 00:42:42,977
We're just as tight
as Na Dae-il and Mr. Kwon.

719
00:42:43,852 --> 00:42:46,063
It's awfully scary to be close to people.

720
00:42:46,146 --> 00:42:49,024
How do make a statement like that
with no emotion at all?

721
00:42:49,108 --> 00:42:50,734
Did you have emotions as an intern?

722
00:42:50,818 --> 00:42:51,944
How about you, huh?

723
00:42:54,113 --> 00:42:56,198
But you have them now, don't you?

724
00:42:57,032 --> 00:42:59,118
He’s making me take
a trip down memory lane.

725
00:42:59,201 --> 00:43:00,703
Listen to me, Park Tae-gyeong.

726
00:43:01,704 --> 00:43:05,165
This guy right here
is just like this guy right here.

727
00:43:05,249 --> 00:43:07,001
- And this guy--
- Nope, count me out.

728
00:43:08,711 --> 00:43:10,379
I don't wanna be compared to you, either!

729
00:43:10,462 --> 00:43:12,798
When I was your age,
I was so much more impressive than you!

730
00:43:12,881 --> 00:43:14,049
- Huh?
- I really was.

731
00:43:14,633 --> 00:43:17,011
- In pretty much every way.
- Sure, sure, sure.

732
00:43:17,094 --> 00:43:18,262
Wow!

733
00:43:19,847 --> 00:43:21,765
Then my future is…

734
00:43:23,475 --> 00:43:24,893
- Huh?
- Huh?

735
00:43:27,229 --> 00:43:28,731
I think I'm gonna go now.

736
00:43:33,152 --> 00:43:34,528
- Um…
- What?

737
00:43:38,866 --> 00:43:40,200
So Na Dae-il will do the surgery?

738
00:43:40,993 --> 00:43:42,536
- Monday morning?
- Yeah.

739
00:43:42,620 --> 00:43:44,246
Wait, why are you waiting so long?

740
00:43:44,747 --> 00:43:46,332
MATH ACADEMY

741
00:43:46,415 --> 00:43:48,834
<i>He said there was something</i>
<i>he had to do this week.</i>

742
00:43:55,257 --> 00:43:58,594
You must be hungry. There's <i>gimbap </i>there.
Make sure to eat that first.

743
00:43:59,428 --> 00:44:00,679
It's tuna <i>gimbap</i>, your favorite.

744
00:44:01,722 --> 00:44:03,015
Tell me everything you wanna eat.

745
00:44:05,267 --> 00:44:07,603
What do you want tomorrow?
Pizza from that place yesterday?

746
00:44:10,773 --> 00:44:12,566
Oh.

747
00:44:16,320 --> 00:44:17,655
Put your seat belt on.

748
00:44:32,628 --> 00:44:33,587
Today is…

749
00:44:34,672 --> 00:44:35,506
Tuesday.

750
00:44:37,508 --> 00:44:40,260
I'm pretty sure he won't be able to last
until next Monday.

751
00:44:40,344 --> 00:44:41,804
KWON CHUNG-HYEON

752
00:44:41,887 --> 00:44:42,888
Huh.

753
00:44:44,014 --> 00:44:45,182
What is this from?

754
00:45:20,134 --> 00:45:21,051
Do you know…

755
00:45:24,096 --> 00:45:26,140
are there are lot of surgeries
scheduled this week?

756
00:45:31,770 --> 00:45:32,855
Dr. Gye Su-jeong!

757
00:45:35,232 --> 00:45:36,775
You walk fast.

758
00:45:37,943 --> 00:45:40,320
When they say you leave work on time,
they're not kidding.

759
00:45:41,238 --> 00:45:44,491
Even though I saw you twice today,
we never got to talk in private.

760
00:45:44,992 --> 00:45:47,745
Mr. Kwon Chung-hyeon
won't be able to last until Monday.

761
00:45:47,828 --> 00:45:49,788
That's not what I want to talk about.

762
00:45:50,372 --> 00:45:51,206
Uh…

763
00:45:53,208 --> 00:45:54,543
Uh…

764
00:45:54,626 --> 00:45:56,086
The thing is, um…

765
00:45:56,879 --> 00:45:57,838
I wanna eat a meal with you.

766
00:46:01,133 --> 00:46:02,843
Ah.

767
00:46:02,926 --> 00:46:05,053
That sounded so lame, I'm embarrassed.

768
00:46:06,597 --> 00:46:09,141
But we should eat.

769
00:46:10,142 --> 00:46:11,101
Together.

770
00:46:11,685 --> 00:46:13,937
Socializing is not something I do.

771
00:46:14,438 --> 00:46:17,191
What if it's not socializing,
what if I wanna talk about work?

772
00:46:17,274 --> 00:46:18,358
Then do it now.

773
00:46:18,442 --> 00:46:20,778
If he needs surgery before Monday,
will you still do it?

774
00:46:20,861 --> 00:46:22,446
If I'm available, then yes.

775
00:46:22,529 --> 00:46:24,698
- What if you aren't?
- Then some other doctor can do it.

776
00:46:26,283 --> 00:46:29,578
- Did you see the imaging? On the liver?
- That's…

777
00:46:29,661 --> 00:46:33,373
most likely just a minor adhesion that
formed due to his surgery years ago.

778
00:46:34,792 --> 00:46:35,959
But you never know.

779
00:46:36,043 --> 00:46:37,628
Well, I doubt that it's a tumor.

780
00:46:37,711 --> 00:46:39,213
You'll have to open him up to find out.

781
00:46:43,759 --> 00:46:47,012
I watched the footage of your surgery.
I've never seen anything like it.

782
00:46:47,638 --> 00:46:49,932
If I were the patient,
I'd want you as my surgeon.

783
00:46:50,933 --> 00:46:52,643
It was truly amazing.

784
00:46:53,227 --> 00:46:55,479
It seemed like you were a god.

785
00:47:01,443 --> 00:47:03,487
Or a monster.

786
00:47:06,240 --> 00:47:07,908
I heard that you leap before you look.

787
00:47:08,659 --> 00:47:10,285
That made me curious as to…

788
00:47:11,495 --> 00:47:12,746
what you’re leaping into.

789
00:47:13,997 --> 00:47:15,249
I leap before I look?

790
00:47:15,332 --> 00:47:17,125
According to Dr. Park Tae-gyeong.

791
00:47:19,378 --> 00:47:20,295
He doesn't know me.

792
00:47:25,217 --> 00:47:26,677
Then is it behind you?

793
00:47:28,011 --> 00:47:31,306
Is there something behind you
that makes you leap before you look?

794
00:47:49,575 --> 00:47:52,202
I guess I don't know Dr. Gye.

795
00:47:55,414 --> 00:47:56,874
Oh, come on.

796
00:48:01,169 --> 00:48:02,504
Ah.

797
00:48:56,975 --> 00:48:57,976
Su-jeong!

798
00:49:02,981 --> 00:49:05,442
Oh, nice! Go make us some money.

799
00:49:08,779 --> 00:49:10,155
WEDNESDAY
8:10 A.M.

800
00:49:10,238 --> 00:49:17,245
WEDNESDAY
8:31 A.M.

801
00:49:18,872 --> 00:49:19,831
Shall we go in?

802
00:49:24,086 --> 00:49:25,087
Thank you, miss!

803
00:49:41,269 --> 00:49:42,104
Go!

804
00:49:42,187 --> 00:49:44,189
WEDNESDAY
7:45 P.M.

805
00:49:44,272 --> 00:49:45,107
Nice.

806
00:50:04,209 --> 00:50:05,877
Next, Choi Ha-il,

807
00:50:06,378 --> 00:50:07,754
a 56-year-old male.

808
00:50:08,296 --> 00:50:11,925
He is a severe alcoholic and has history
of drinking two bottles of soju per day.

809
00:50:12,009 --> 00:50:15,971
He was diagnosed with cirrhosis
of the liver, but was lost to follow-up.

810
00:50:17,639 --> 00:50:21,810
He reportedly developed jaundice
a month ago and ascites about a week ago,

811
00:50:21,893 --> 00:50:23,562
which prompted his visit to the ER.

812
00:50:24,312 --> 00:50:25,814
Tests performed upon admission

813
00:50:25,897 --> 00:50:27,899
showed uncompensated liver cirrhosis,

814
00:50:27,983 --> 00:50:31,153
Child-Pugh Class C,
and a MELD score of 34.

815
00:50:31,236 --> 00:50:33,113
He is expected to undergo
a liver transplant.

816
00:50:33,196 --> 00:50:39,995
THURSDAY
3:31 P.M.

817
00:50:43,957 --> 00:50:47,210
THURSDAY
3:32 P.M.

818
00:50:47,294 --> 00:50:53,467
FRIDAY
5:44 P.M.

819
00:51:01,016 --> 00:51:02,517
Is this my seat?

820
00:51:06,063 --> 00:51:08,732
You know, I've loved seaweed soup
since I was a kid.

821
00:51:08,815 --> 00:51:14,488
FRIDAY
7:38 P.M.

822
00:51:14,571 --> 00:51:19,576
FRIDAY
7:39 P.M.

823
00:51:19,659 --> 00:51:20,952
Huh? What the--

824
00:51:24,915 --> 00:51:25,749
DAD

825
00:51:26,875 --> 00:51:27,876
Come on, pick up.

826
00:51:32,881 --> 00:51:39,888
FRIDAY
7:50 P.M.

827
00:51:42,307 --> 00:51:45,727
All right, let us raise a glass to
Dr. Na Dae-il. A toast to a new beginning!

828
00:51:45,811 --> 00:51:47,354
Cheers!

829
00:51:47,979 --> 00:51:49,815
Please take good care of me.

830
00:51:51,983 --> 00:51:53,693
"Please take good care of me."

831
00:51:54,361 --> 00:51:55,737
I wanna thank you all

832
00:51:55,821 --> 00:51:59,616
for giving me this precious gold
Magnolia badge.

833
00:52:00,325 --> 00:52:02,786
I always wanted one of these.

834
00:52:03,870 --> 00:52:06,623
FRIDAY
8:15 P.M.

835
00:52:06,706 --> 00:52:07,958
- Dad?
- Get out.

836
00:52:15,257 --> 00:52:16,591
Dad, what about my after-school class?

837
00:52:16,675 --> 00:52:18,051
DR. JO GUK-JIN
ME & LIFE PLASTIC SURGERY

838
00:52:19,511 --> 00:52:21,346
I'm swamped right now.
You'll have to miss it.

839
00:52:23,098 --> 00:52:24,349
I need an ambulance.

840
00:52:24,432 --> 00:52:26,226
- I'm in front of Taeseong Academy.
- Please!

841
00:52:26,309 --> 00:52:29,771
FRIDAY
8:16 P.M.

842
00:52:30,272 --> 00:52:32,107
FRIDAY
8:55 P.M.

843
00:52:35,068 --> 00:52:36,403
MARCH 20, 2026
FRIDAY, 8:55 P.M.

844
00:52:40,490 --> 00:52:42,659
What are you still doing here?

845
00:52:43,368 --> 00:52:45,954
This is the ER at Seonam Medical Center.

846
00:52:46,037 --> 00:52:48,456
The driver of a dump truck
fell asleep at the wheel.

847
00:52:48,540 --> 00:52:49,958
We have 20 patients at the scene,

848
00:52:50,041 --> 00:52:52,544
but we've only brought 12 here so far.
More on the way.

849
00:52:52,627 --> 00:52:54,588
Dr. Kim, Dr. Kim!
Take this patient, please!

850
00:52:55,755 --> 00:52:58,842
Clear out the minor injuries to make room,
empty the treatment room,

851
00:52:58,925 --> 00:53:01,386
and move any stable critical care patients
to the general ward.

852
00:53:01,469 --> 00:53:03,513
And page the interns, right now.

853
00:53:03,597 --> 00:53:05,432
- Will do.
- Dr. Gye, this patient--

854
00:53:05,515 --> 00:53:07,142
All interns to the ER.

855
00:53:19,654 --> 00:53:21,781
Uh, Chairman, excuse me for one moment.

856
00:53:25,952 --> 00:53:28,413
Hello, Dr. Kim. How can I help you?

857
00:53:29,748 --> 00:53:30,582
Sorry?

858
00:53:32,918 --> 00:53:34,377
Ah, yes, Mr. Kwon.

859
00:53:36,046 --> 00:53:37,380
Okay, I'll be there soon.

860
00:53:37,964 --> 00:53:42,177
Although, I'm out at the moment and I
don't know if I'll make it there in time.

861
00:53:42,260 --> 00:53:43,887
Maybe there's another doctor available.

862
00:53:47,349 --> 00:53:48,850
Really? Dr. Gye?

863
00:53:49,476 --> 00:53:50,727
But… why her?

864
00:53:53,480 --> 00:53:55,273
I doubt she's available right now.

865
00:53:55,357 --> 00:53:57,150
Yeah, there's no one else who can do it.

866
00:53:57,234 --> 00:53:59,152
The ER's out of control.
There was a major car accident.

867
00:53:59,236 --> 00:54:00,779
All the other doctors are down here,

868
00:54:00,862 --> 00:54:03,073
- so she's getting ready to do the surgery…
- Yes, just a moment.

869
00:54:03,156 --> 00:54:04,282
What?

870
00:54:05,116 --> 00:54:06,034
<i>I can't hear you.</i>

871
00:54:06,910 --> 00:54:08,912
<i>Mr. Kwon's fever is too high right now.</i>

872
00:54:08,995 --> 00:54:11,248
Sorry, what can't be done?

873
00:54:11,331 --> 00:54:13,708
What? Uh, excuse me, Dr. Na? Hang on.

874
00:54:14,960 --> 00:54:16,294
Dr. Gye, what's going on?

875
00:54:17,212 --> 00:54:18,088
What?

876
00:54:18,588 --> 00:54:20,966
You can't get in the OR?
The fingerprint scanner doesn't work?

877
00:54:21,675 --> 00:54:22,759
Why isn't it working?

878
00:54:22,842 --> 00:54:24,302
Uh, just hang on a minute.

879
00:54:24,761 --> 00:54:26,346
Dr. Na, right now, uh--

880
00:54:26,429 --> 00:54:28,056
When was the last time you hit the links?

881
00:54:28,139 --> 00:54:32,018
- Oh, I try to play once or twice a month.
- There's also a good course here.

882
00:54:32,102 --> 00:54:34,437
Wow, I'd love to, just let me know when.

883
00:54:35,188 --> 00:54:38,108
- Save it for the next meeting.
- Come to my place.

884
00:54:38,191 --> 00:54:41,945
Dr. Gye! Dr. Gye!
I heard you need my finger--

885
00:54:42,028 --> 00:54:43,905
There we go.

886
00:54:46,032 --> 00:54:47,033
You, assist me.

887
00:54:47,117 --> 00:54:47,993
Oh, okay. Coming.

888
00:54:48,785 --> 00:54:50,245
Isn't there anyone else available?

889
00:54:50,328 --> 00:54:51,663
Only Dr. Jo Won-jin.

890
00:54:51,746 --> 00:54:53,456
They're all downstairs
because of the accident.

891
00:54:53,540 --> 00:54:56,876
I don't want to wait for an assistant,
so you'll do. I want to do it right away.

892
00:54:59,838 --> 00:55:00,672
Or no?

893
00:55:00,755 --> 00:55:03,049
I'll do it.

894
00:55:06,553 --> 00:55:07,595
Uh…

895
00:55:11,766 --> 00:55:15,812
I can't believe those surgeons!
Deleting your fingerprint registration?

896
00:55:15,895 --> 00:55:18,773
Also, I could've just gone out and opened
the door. Why'd you chase after her?

897
00:55:21,985 --> 00:55:23,570
Oh, you're opening him up?

898
00:55:23,653 --> 00:55:25,655
There's severe adhesion. And what else?

899
00:55:25,739 --> 00:55:27,824
I'll have to open him up to find out.

900
00:55:42,088 --> 00:55:43,381
<i>This is Kim Seong-jin.</i>

901
00:55:43,465 --> 00:55:45,508
<i>We're opening him up.</i>
<i>There's likely to be severe adhesion.</i>

902
00:55:45,592 --> 00:55:48,845
<i>Dr. Gye Su-jeong will take care of him,</i>
<i>so I don't think we'll need you here.</i>

903
00:55:53,683 --> 00:55:55,560
I have to go do an emergency surgery.

904
00:55:55,643 --> 00:55:57,479
Oh, of course. We understand.

905
00:55:57,562 --> 00:55:59,314
What's with him?

906
00:56:04,486 --> 00:56:05,570
Bovie.

907
00:56:06,488 --> 00:56:07,530
Bovie.

908
00:56:39,771 --> 00:56:44,401
Man. There was a huge accident.
Traffic is at a standstill.

909
00:56:44,484 --> 00:56:45,944
We're gonna be here for a while.

910
00:57:01,209 --> 00:57:04,421
DR. NA DAE-IL

911
00:58:02,228 --> 00:58:03,730
Damn it, Gye Su-jeong.

912
00:58:39,307 --> 00:58:40,475
Huh.

913
00:59:26,437 --> 00:59:29,399
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

914
01:00:14,527 --> 01:00:17,488
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

915
01:00:19,032 --> 01:00:21,534
<i>They're initials, right?</i>
<i>I'm not the only one who sees this, right?</i>

916
01:00:21,618 --> 01:00:23,286
<i>- You'll let the hospital know?</i>
- <i>No.</i>

917
01:00:23,369 --> 01:00:24,871
This hospital brought him in.

918
01:00:24,954 --> 01:00:28,583
<i>Why did you show me the picture?</i>
<i>There's nothing I can do.</i>

919
01:00:28,666 --> 01:00:30,084
Get away from him. He's my patient.

920
01:00:30,585 --> 01:00:33,171
<i>He's alive, thanks to you.</i>
<i>It's such a relief.</i>

921
01:00:33,755 --> 01:00:35,673
<i>I wish you hadn't said that.</i>

922
01:00:35,757 --> 01:00:36,883
Where is she? Your teacher.

923
01:00:36,966 --> 01:00:40,011
<i>I think the time</i>
<i>has truly come to terminate the contract.</i>

924
01:00:40,595 --> 01:00:44,932
Don't worry.
One thing's for sure, I never fail.
